  "summary": "A candidate for the Yavapai College District Governing Board, Ryan Jones, has placed about 70 campaign-style signs under Flock ALPR cameras around Prescott, Arizona, reading 'Flock Cam Here' and 'Private AI Cams Tracking YOU' to protest mass surveillance. The article notes the signs are legal under Arizona campaign-sign law and mentions Tempe City Council's vote the same day to permanently ban ALPR technology.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "It is absolutely a cheap stunt to get attention to my campaign, but it's also calling attention to a bigger issue",
      "paragraph_idx": 0
    },
    {
      "quote": "A police officer who I don't know, in Nebraska let's say, can look up my license plate and see where I've been for 7 to 30 days",
      "paragraph_idx": 0
    },
    {
      "quote": "On Thursday, Tempe city council voted to permanently ban the city from ever using ALPR technology.",
      "paragraph_idx": 0
    }
